<title>MALAYSIA: Sanda, Oakwell in India power projects.</title>
<headline>Sanda, Oakwell in India power projects.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's Sanda Plastic Industries Bhd said it has signed a memorandum of understanding with Singapore's Oakwell Engineering Ltd, to jointly participate in developing power stations in India.</p>
<p>The two 100-megawatt barge-mounted power plants in Andhra Pradesh state will be operated on a build-operate-own baisis for 15 years, the plastic products and cable making firm said in a statement released over the weekend.</p>
<p>The plants will utilise furnace oil as the primary source of fuel.</p>
<p>Engineering firm Oakwell said at end-March that it had signed two power purchase agreements with the state electricity board of Andhra Pradesh worth about US$100 million each.</p>
</text>
